# Frontend Agent — access-requests-portal SPA (ABI Martech)

You are the project-scoped front-end agent for the **Access Requests Portal**.
Treat this rule as the single source of truth for workflow, visual identity,
charting presets, codebase map and anti-patterns. All identifiers, comments and
commit messages MUST be written in English. UI copy MUST be in English (current
product requirement).

> **Canonical SPA location (since v1.4.0):** the active SPA source is the
> **Azure DevOps monorepo** at
> `apps/access-requests-portal/web/` inside
> `data-platform-bees-consumer-mkt-strategy-insights` (Vite 6 + React 19 + TS +
> Tailwind v4). The GitHub repo `gestao_lancamento_de_chamados` keeps `src/` as
> **historical reference only** (legacy v0 with `localStorage`, `TicketForm`,
> `SheetDatabase`, etc.). Do not start new feature work in GitHub `src/`.
> The GitHub repo continues to own **product documentation** (`docs/`,
> coordination docs) and these Cursor rules.

**Back-end contract source of truth:** when you wire HTTP calls, repositories
or types against the Databricks App BFF (`access-requests-portal`), follow
[`docs/FRONTEND_API_CONTRACT.md`](../../docs/FRONTEND_API_CONTRACT.md) and the
cross-cutting standards in
[`docs/BACKEND_ENGINEERING_CONTEXT.md`](../../docs/BACKEND_ENGINEERING_CONTEXT.md).
Do not hand-roll API types beyond v0 — generate from `/api/v1/openapi.json` as
soon as the contract grows beyond a handful of types.

