## 3. Design direction — ABI Martech engineering portal (binding)

The visual identity is a **dark engineering portal** modeled on the internal
ABI Martech Data Quality Portal (ADO repo `martech-data-quality-portal`):
- Dense, information-rich layouts in the spirit of Linear/Datadog/Grafana but
  with ABI Martech accents.
- Indigo as primary action, cyan as highlight/selection, slate-950 as canvas.
- Soft-fill status pills, fixed sidebar shell, focused gradient touches in
  chrome only (logo halo, hero KPI cards) — never on whole pages or buttons.

### Reference repo (study patterns, do not copy code wholesale)

Local checkout:
`C:\Users\gperuzzf\OneDrive - NTT DATA EMEAL\Documentos\ABI\GHQ_B2B_Delta\martech-data-quality-portal`

Re-read for tone and component shape:
- `src/index.css` (CSS vars, scrollbar, animations, focus styles).
- `src/components/layout/{Header,Sidebar}.tsx` (shell + gradient halo logo).
- `src/components/ui/{StatusBadge,Skeleton,Toast}.tsx` (primitives).
- `src/views/ConsistencyView.tsx` (chart + cards + modal patterns).

### Do adopt

- **Dark-first shell** (`bg-slate-950 text-slate-200`). Optional light theme via
  `:root.light` CSS vars (parity is a later concern).
- **Fixed sidebar** (`w-20` mobile / `w-64` md+), `bg-slate-900 border-r
  border-slate-800`. Grouped nav with sub-items; active group in
  `indigo-600/10 + indigo-400 + indigo-600/20 border`, active sub-item in
  `text-cyan-400 bg-cyan-500/5`.
- **Header** with bold H1, supporting paragraph, primary Refresh button in
  `bg-indigo-600 hover:bg-indigo-700 text-white`. Secondary buttons:
  `bg-slate-900 border border-slate-700 rounded-lg text-slate-400 hover:text-white`.
- **Cards**: `bg-slate-800/50 border border-slate-700 rounded-xl p-4–5`.
  Hero/highlighted cards may use `bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-800/80
  to-slate-900/80`. Active/selected card: `ring-2 ring-cyan-500/20` (or
  `indigo-500/30`) instead of stronger borders.
- **Soft-fill status badges**: `{color}-500/10` bg + `{color}-400` text +
  `{color}-500/20` border, always paired with an icon and a label.
- **Targeted gradients only** in chrome:
  - Logo halo: `from-indigo-500 via-cyan-500 to-emerald-500 ... blur-sm`.
  - Brand title text: `bg-clip-text text-transparent` over a slate→white
    gradient.
  - Charts: linear gradient defs filling areas under cyan/indigo lines.
- **Modals**: full-screen overlay `bg-black/60 backdrop-blur-sm`, dialog
  `bg-slate-800 border border-slate-700 rounded-xl shadow-2xl`.
- **Animations (CSS-only, all respect `prefers-reduced-motion`)**:
  `animate-pulse-slow`, `fade-in`, `slide-in-right`, `shimmer`. Focus ring
  `outline: 2px solid #6366f1` (indigo-500).
- **Density**: dense tables, `text-xs`/`text-[11px]`/`text-[10px]` for
  metadata, `JetBrains Mono` for IDs and numeric/aligned columns.
- **Accessibility**: skip-link, focus-visible outlines, never color alone (pair
  label + icon), WCAG 2.2 AA contrast on the dark canvas (check small text on
  `slate-800/50`).

### Do NOT introduce

- Apple-like glassmorphism on layout chrome (`backdrop-filter` on the page or
  sidebar). `backdrop-blur-sm` is allowed **only** on modal/overlay scrim.
- Multi-radial ambient gradients painted on the whole canvas.
- Marketing hero typography (`clamp(2.4rem, 5.4vw, 4.8rem)`), gradient-fill
  buttons, transform-based hover lifts (`hover:scale-105`,
  `hover:translate-y-…`).
- `rounded-2xl`/`rounded-3xl` or fully circular decorative shapes (badges and
  avatars excepted).
- `shadow-lg`+ outside modal dialog containers and the notification panel. No
  colored hover shadows on regular cards.
- Animated decorative orbs/loaders. Spinners are OK for in-flight states; the
  primary loading pattern is **skeleton**.
- New brand colors outside the slate / indigo / cyan / emerald / amber / rose
  / sky family without a token update in §4 first.
- Three or more competing accents in the same region (pick indigo OR cyan as
  the dominant accent per card/section).

