## 6. Anti-patterns to flag in reviews

Reject or rewrite any PR that does the following:

- Reintroduces `firebase`, `express`, `dotenv`, `@google/genai` (or any
  AI-vendor SDK) in the SPA.
- Persists credentials or tokens in `localStorage`. The legacy
  `SheetDatabase.tsx` does this — it is frozen and **must not be ported**
  without rewriting its persistence layer onto the BFF.
- Grows `SheetDatabase.tsx`, `TicketForm.tsx` or `TicketForm2.tsx` in the
  GitHub legacy tree. New ticket logic lands in ADO `web/`.
- Adds Apple-style glassmorphism on layout chrome (`backdrop-filter` on
  body/sidebar), multi-radial page gradients, gradient-fill buttons, hero
  marketing typography, transform-based hover lifts, or decorative orb
  loaders.
- Adds `rounded-2xl`/`rounded-3xl`, `shadow-lg`+ on non-modal surfaces,
  colored hover shadows, or `shadow-*` ring stacking on cards.
- Introduces hex codes outside the slate / indigo / cyan / emerald / amber /
  rose / sky palette without first updating §4 in this rule.
- Adds Recharts charts with vertical `CartesianGrid`, visible tick lines on
  both axes, light theme tooltip on the dark canvas, oversized legends, or
  pie/donut with 5+ slices.
- Adds a new top-level route or screen without honoring the sidebar/header
  shell (fixed sidebar 80/256px, env badge top-right, header with H1 +
  subtitle).
- Hand-writes new BFF response types when the contract already exposes them
  via `/api/v1/openapi.json` (generate them; do not drift the contract).
- Modifies ADO shared infra files (`app.yaml`, `requirements.txt`,
  `.gitignore`, `workspace_auth.py`, `ticket_models.py`) without an explicit
  task that requires it.

